{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"b53060bf6fc3866d165522b05e4a34deece677f61b1db0444e6295059779b90b","digest":{"component_or_area":"event store SIGNATURE record storage + op-cert producer/reducer","key_entities":["reducer/_processors.py::process_signature","signing.sign_opcert_manifest","signing.sign_manifest","opcert.sign_opcert","opcert.opcert_from_record","opcert.verify_opcert","dsse.encode","dsse.Envelope","SIGNATURE event","attestations[kind]","material_fingerprint","merged_log_commit","envelope","algorithm=sshsig","TAG_DELTA"],"problem_keywords":["op-cert","dsse envelope","attestation storage","event sourcing","signature event","reducer","compaction survival","hmac migration","asymmetric signing","additive schema evolution","rollout compatibility"],"propositions":["An asymmetric op-cert DSSE envelope must be stored on a ticket by extending the existing SIGNATURE event record rather than introducing a new event type.","The producer signing.sign_opcert_manifest writes a SIGNATURE event carrying the DSSE envelope plus bound material_fingerprint and merged_log_commit, omitting the HMAC signature/algorithm.","The reducer process_signature must preserve envelope, material_fingerprint, and merged_log_commit into the attestations[kind] record present-only, surviving a compact-then-replay round-trip unchanged.","opcert.opcert_from_record returns (envelope, bound_fields) for an op-cert record and None for a legacy HMAC record, and the returned envelope verifies via opcert.verify_opcert with a pinned keyring.","The record-schema extension is additive so legacy HMAC sign_manifest records remain byte-unchanged and still HMAC-verify.","Op-cert SIGNATURE events are preserved append-only but read as unsigned on pre-upgrade clones lacking an asymmetric verifier, so verify/reconcile hosts must be upgraded first."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785204816016332942,"uuid":"e4f6d9d4-794b-4d89-84da-a0802363a8c1"}